    "created_at": "2015-11-25T01:43:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-25T01:43:58Z",
    "body": "FWIW - I think this is a bit different than `only-if-cached`. The problem there is that it makes it possible to probe the cache without any corresponding traffic being emitted to the server, making it a passive attack. \n\nExposing `fromCache` doesn't do that; if someone tries to use it for probing, it will still emit traffic. \n\nWhat it does do is _slightly_ improve confidence as opposed to cache timing attacks (but they're pretty conclusive anyway, AIUI).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
